{"body":"The Batch 10 #601 author observed a distinct failure before the scroll round trip on unchanged accepted source `f6c31e271297eece52f34102dc40a1e2ed7069a8` (tree `69ddfad6deb814dd08fdaee2db2d512d73e14c78`). Clicking pagination button 2 rendered rows 11–20, but the URL remained `/counties`; the original `gotoPageNOfCountiesList` URL assertion failed at `frontend/e2e/smart-back.spec.ts:38` after 5000ms. The test never reached scrollTo or county/detail/back navigation.\n\nActual local Linux AMD64 production-config Chromium replay: Playwright 1.58.2, Chromium 145.0.7632.6, Node 22.23.3 x64, viewport 1280×720, two workers, zero retries, 100 original-case attempts: 99 passes / 1 unexpected failure. Docker Desktop runs under macOS ARM64 emulation; this is not hosted or deployed acceptance. The failure trace shows a successful 200 request for `/counties?p=2&_rsc=…`, followed by snapshots/URL assertions still at `/counties`. No causal explanation is established.\n\nPreserved raw report/log/trace/screenshot/video and executable archive checks are in the author handoff branch `codex/batch10-county-scroll`, `docs/admin/implementation/batch10-scroll-evidence/`. Trace SHA-256: `632bd83708061ba281d908c4b1ad40acb4db5707277ce8f88ca5b150b8cc9585`. The branch is an unresolved investigation handoff, not a repair PR. #601's historical post-back Y=100 failure remains separate and unresolved.\n\nAcceptance: reproduce the URL/table disagreement with causal router/history/hydration observations; preserve the original failed attempt; fix the demonstrated cause while maintaining page/deep-link/filter/back/forward behavior; demonstrate an actual failing control then a pass and rerun the original complete Chromium inventory with no unexpected or retried failures. Do not weaken assertions, add sleeps or quarantine the prerequisite.\n\nDeduplication: fresh complete all-state REST census (298 issues across seven pages, PRs excluded), plus pagination/county/URL searches. #221 concerns earlier SSR/LCP work, #291 original browser verification, #601 post-back scroll restoration; no dedicated current page-2 URL/table mismatch ticket was found. No app/test/config/dependency change or deployed mutation was made.\n","comments":[],"number":607,"state":"OPEN","title":"P2: County Explorer page 2 intermittently renders without updating its URL","url":"https://github.com/Rodgers31/audit_app/issues/607"}
